#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:1
msgid "Schemas and Memory Decay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:3
msgid "Atomic Fact Schema (items.yaml)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:20
msgid "Memory Decay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:22
msgid ""
"Facts decay in retrieval priority over time so stale info does not crowd "
"out recent context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:24
msgid ""
"**Access tracking:** When a fact is used in conversation, bump "
"`access_count` and set `last_accessed` to today. During heartbeat "
"extraction, scan the session for referenced entity facts and update their"
" access metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:26
msgid "**Recency tiers (for summary.md rewriting):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:28
msgid "**Hot** (accessed in last 7 days) -- include prominently in summary.md."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:29
msgid "**Warm** (8-30 days ago) -- include at lower priority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:30
msgid ""
"**Cold** (30+ days or never accessed) -- omit from summary.md. Still in "
"items.yaml, retrievable on demand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:31
msgid ""
"High `access_count` resists decay -- frequently used facts stay warm "
"longer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:33
msgid ""
"**Weekly synthesis:** Sort by recency tier, then by access_count within "
"tier. Cold facts drop out of the summary but remain in items.yaml. "
"Accessing a cold fact reheats it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_schemas.md:35
msgid ""
"No deletion. Decay only affects retrieval priority via summary.md "
"curation. The full record always lives in items.yaml."
msgstr ""

